        <body>
            <trans-unit id="m0zKYk1">
                <source>description.guided_project_crowdfunding_blocks</source>
                <target>Everything the form's fields do not say is written in blocks, with the same editor the site's pages are composed with.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="LqUplER">
                <source>description.guided_project_crowdfunding_campaign</source>
                <target>The goal, the dates, the presentation and the author: what a campaign is before it has anything to offer.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="Bo1XOJ3">
                <source>description.guided_project_crowdfunding_counterpart</source>
                <target>What a contributor gets in return for their gift, with its amount and, where there is one, the number of copies available.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id=".E7he3K">
                <source>description.guided_project_crowdfunding_draw_video</source>
                <target>Once the draw has been filmed, the video goes on the lottery or, if the file is too heavy, on the campaign with a YouTube address.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="rFPdrwq">
                <source>description.guided_project_crowdfunding_lottery</source>
                <target>A draw date and prizes. Tickets are sold like counterparts, and the draw happens on the lottery's public page.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="urDtbec">
                <source>description.guided_project_crowdfunding_media</source>
                <target>The photographs and videos of the public page: a campaign nobody sees is a campaign nobody funds.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="wJ18L1_">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_blocks_add</source>
                <target>The "Blocks" section, at the very bottom of the form. Texts, pictures, buttons, tables: the same as a page of the site's, and they move around the same way.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="gxuhOnD">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_blocks_done</source>
                <target>The blocks show on the public page, below the presentation and the counterparts.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="DDEqPtb">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_blocks_edit</source>
                <target>The pencil, on the row of the campaign to fill in.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="kmrhQv4">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_blocks_open</source>
                <target>A campaign's blocks are composed on its sheet, below the fields describing it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="6pMhcxi">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_campaign_author</source>
                <target>Who carries the project. The name, the presentation and the website appear together on the page: a contributor gives to somebody, not to a pot.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="8pFJAvy">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_campaign_dates</source>
                <target>The campaign only takes contributions between these two dates. Before, and after, its counterparts can no longer be added to the basket.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="HRKqvMA">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_campaign_description</source>
                <target>The opening text, at the top of the public page. Say in a few lines what you want to do and why; the detail is composed further down, in blocks.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="fHTZh3T">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_campaign_done</source>
                <target>The campaign is online as soon as it exists, and visible between its two dates. The parcours that follow fill it in: its pictures, its counterparts, its lottery.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="_M0S4bg">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_campaign_goal</source>
                <target>The amount to reach. It is what the public page's gauge compares the contributions already received to.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="L5sz.S5">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_campaign_new</source>
                <target>The button above the list opens an empty form. It carries everything: the campaign, its media, its counterparts, its lottery and its blocks.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="8E51Ewv">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_campaign_open</source>
                <target>Every campaign of the site is listed here, the one ending latest first.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="8MwwlvA">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_campaign_slug</source>
                <target>It fills itself in from the title. Once the campaign has been shared, leave it alone: the links already out there would stop working.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="jpUn2Je">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_campaign_title</source>
                <target>It is the name the campaign appears under everywhere: in the list, on its page, in the basket and in the emails sent to contributors.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="QQuS8Ai">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_counterpart_add</source>
                <target>The "Counterparts" section. Give it a title, an amount and a description: it is what a contributor reads before choosing.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id=".x5B8xo">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_counterpart_done</source>
                <target>The counterpart is added to the basket like any other item. The shop is what takes the money: this bundle never handles it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="BKuv7RS">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_counterpart_edit</source>
                <target>The pencil, on the row of the campaign the counterpart belongs to.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="J25OJ4u">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_counterpart_expand</source>
                <target>A counterpart once added folds onto its title. Open it: the price, the limited quantity and the expected delivery are all inside.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="qWM59CT">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_counterpart_open</source>
                <target>A counterpart belongs to a campaign and is created on its sheet: there is no counterparts screen.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="_0dRlZp">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_counterpart_quantity</source>
                <target>A limited quantity takes the counterpart off sale once it runs out, and the basket refuses to order more than what is left. Leave zero not to limit it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="pBi5ebg">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_draw_video_done</source>
                <target>The winners have already had their email, sent at the moment of the draw. The video is what everybody else sees: it remains to be announced, by hand, on social networks.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="nozqyBG">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_draw_video_edit</source>
                <target>The pencil, on the row of the campaign whose lottery has just been drawn.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="uJINwgx">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_draw_video_lottery</source>
                <target>The "Lottery" section, the one you have just drawn. Open it: its "Videos" field is folded up inside.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="yUyQkUz">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_draw_video_open</source>
                <target>The draw's video goes on the campaign carrying the lottery, like everything else.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="LjfF0xf">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_draw_video_upload</source>
                <target>Its "Videos" field only takes an uploaded file. The video then shows under the prizes, on the draw's own page, where contributors go looking for it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="vEi1b6q">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_draw_video_youtube</source>
                <target>For a file too heavy: publish it on YouTube, then paste its address into the campaign's videos, in the "Media" section. It is the only one of the two fields taking an address.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="13LRffH">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_lottery_add</source>
                <target>The "Lottery" section. Tick "Enable" and set the draw's date: the draw button stays greyed out until it has passed.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="l5evlUU">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_lottery_done</source>
                <target>The draw itself does not happen here: it takes place on the lottery's public page, at the date set, and you alone see the button there. Film it: the "Film and publish a lottery draw" procedure says how, and why there is no second take.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="inMyLuT">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_lottery_edit</source>
                <target>The pencil, on the row of the campaign carrying the lottery.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="kTuxs8s">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_lottery_expand</source>
                <target>A lottery once added folds onto its title. Open it: "Enable", the identifier, the draw's date and the prizes are all inside.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="sWi8KFW">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_lottery_open</source>
                <target>A lottery belongs to a campaign: its tickets are contributions, and its draw rewards those who gave.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="yv7V5uv">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_lottery_prizes</source>
                <target>One prize per rank, from the first to the last. A ticket only wins once: a ticket already drawn is taken out of the draws that follow.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="PvP917x">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_media_done</source>
                <target>The public page shows your pictures. Nothing more to publish: what is saved is online.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="zOOKTt9">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_media_edit</source>
                <target>The pencil, on the row of the campaign to illustrate.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="OyJ02qF">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_media_open</source>
                <target>A campaign's pictures go on its own sheet: it is a single form, where everything composing it holds together.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="eZVMvUv">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_media_photos</source>
                <target>The "Media" section. Every picture added shows on the public page, in the order you put them in. The first one is the one seen first.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="h8uTQLk">
                <source>description.guided_step_crowdfunding_media_videos</source>
                <target>Just below. A campaign video takes an uploaded file or, more simply, a YouTube address: that is the way to go for a heavy file.</target>
            </trans-unit>
